## What it does

`apps/web` is the reader site. It is one Foldkit program.
Foldkit is a UI framework on Effect: a Model, Messages, an `update` function, and a pure view.

Server rendering means the Worker builds the page HTML for each request.
Prerendering means the build writes page HTML to files before deployment.
Hydration means the browser program adopts HTML that the server rendered and continues from it.

One `vite build` makes three outputs:

- The browser bundle that hydrates each page.
- The server `fetch` function that Foldkit generates from `src/entry.server.ts`.
- One HTML file for each path in the server entry's `prerenderPaths` export.

`Cloudflare.Website.Foldkit` deploys the outputs as one Worker. A request for a prerendered page gets the file. Any other request goes to the server `fetch` function. It renders the page, an error page, or a 404 with its real status.

The server forwards `/rpc` to the private RpcBackend Worker. Browser Commands call capabilities through that path.

Each reader page has three panes:

- The section index lists the pages in the current section and marks the current page.
- The page holds the body, its "Referenced by" cards, and the phone outline.
- The rail holds the outline of the page headings and the local graph of linked pages.

Hovering or focusing an internal link opens a peek card with the target's title and summary. The card reads the page through the `read` capability and caches the result.

The settings panel changes theme, prose font, size, measure, and accent. A small head script applies the saved settings before the first paint, so the page does not flash.

## The standard

- `vite.config.ts` turns on rendering with one `foldkit({ ssr })` call. It uses the default `dist/client` and `dist/server` directories.
- The server entry exports `renderPage`, `renderDocument`, and `prerenderPaths`.
- Every finite public page is prerendered. Pages that depend on the request render on the server.
- Readable content and links work before browser JavaScript runs.
- A missing page returns a real 404. It never falls back to the home page.
- Production builds contain no development modules, devtools code, or test people.
- Without JavaScript, the reader still works. Links are plain anchors, the phone outline is a native `details` element, and graph nodes are SVG links.
- Peek cards, graph hover, and the menu need JavaScript. They add to the page and never replace a link.
- Pink accent marks wiki structure only. `AGENTS.md` lists the allowed uses.
- The content security policy allows one inline script: the settings head script, by its hash.
- Remote state lives in the Model. Views read the Model and send Messages; they never fetch.
- Escape closes the menu and the settings panel and returns focus to the button that opened them.

## How to check

- Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/web build`. Read `apps/web/dist/server/foldkit.build.json`. It names `fetch.js` as the server entry and lists the prerendered paths.
- Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/web test` for page parity and the production-bundle exclusion test. The `*.scene.test.ts` files drive the reader panes, peek, menu, settings, and references through Messages.
- `apps/web/test/reader-csp.test.ts` checks that the policy hash matches the settings head script.
- Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/site test`. `accent.test.ts` holds the allowed accent selectors. `code-contrast.test.ts` checks code token contrast on each code surface in both themes.
- Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/infra test`. The Website build test builds through [Alchemy](/skills/learn-alchemy), reads prerendered pages, and serves them, `/rpc`, and a 404 from the server bundle in workerd.
- On a preview, request a prerendered page and an unknown path with `curl`. The page returns complete HTML with `X-Preview-Commit`. The unknown path returns 404.
